rsync -aogpvz \
  --delete \
  --progress \
  --human-readable \
  -e "ssh -p 20202" \
  --rsync-path="sudo rsync" \
  /var/www/html/ \
  druser@192.168.1.20:/mnt/dr-backup/html/


| Option                                     | Description                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `-a`                                       | Archive mode (preserves symlinks, permissions, ownerships, timestamps)         |
| `-o`                                       | Preserve owner (requires `sudo rsync` on the DR server)                        |
| `-g`                                       | Preserve group                                                                 |
| `-p`                                       | Preserve permissions                                                           |
| `-v`                                       | Verbose (shows file list)                                                      |
| `-z`                                       | Compress data during transfer                                                  |
| `--delete`                                 | Deletes files on DR that don’t exist on Prod (mirror effect)                   |
| `--progress`                               | Shows progress of each file transfer                                           |
| `--human-readable`                         | Displays sizes in MB/GB instead of bytes                                       |
| `-e "ssh -p 20202"`                        | Uses SSH over port `20202`                                                     |
| `--rsync-path="sudo rsync"`                | Runs `rsync` with `sudo` on the DR server (useful if target dir is root-owned) |
| `/var/www/html/`                           | Source directory (trailing `/` means "contents of")                            |
| `druser@192.168.1.20:/mnt/dr-backup/html/` | Destination on the DR server                                                   |


Warning (before running)
Make sure druser has passwordless sudo access to rsync on the DR server:

druser ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/rsync


Ensure the destination path exists (/mnt/dr-backup/html/) or create it with:

sudo mkdir -p /mnt/dr-backup/html
sudo chown druser /mnt/dr-backup/html


